Situation
As part of CBA’s REX modernization project, we were migrating 200+ Tableau dashboards and Pega workflows to a microservices-based cloud architecture. A major bottleneck in the development process was the manual deployment process, which led to:
❌ Frequent deployment failures due to human errors.
❌ Slow release cycles, delaying feature delivery.
❌ Lack of visibility, making it difficult to track deployment status and failures.

Task
I needed to:
✔ Automate the deployment process to ensure efficiency, reliability, and quality.
✔ Implement a CI/CD pipeline that integrated automated testing, monitoring, and rapid feedback.
✔ Foster collaboration between developers, testers, and DevOps teams to streamline deployments.

Action
Following CBA’s leadership principles, I took a structured approach to automation:

1️⃣ CI/CD Pipeline Implementation (Create Exceptional Teams)

Designed and implemented a CI/CD pipeline using GitHub Actions and AWS CodePipeline for deploying Next.js frontend, Java Spring Boot backend, and Snowflake database changes.

Integrated automated testing (unit, integration, and security tests) into the pipeline.

Used infrastructure as code (Terraform) to ensure consistent and repeatable cloud deployments.

2️⃣ Automated Testing & Rapid Feedback (Obsess Over Customers)

Unit tests (Jest for frontend, JUnit for backend) executed on every pull request.

Integration tests validated API endpoints and database interactions.

Static code analysis & security scans (SonarQube, Snyk) ensured code quality and compliance.

Slack notifications provided real-time feedback on pipeline status.

3️⃣ Monitoring & Continuous Improvement

Set up logging and monitoring (AWS CloudWatch, ELK stack) for tracking deployment issues.

Established automated rollback strategies to prevent downtime.

Conducted post-mortem reviews to analyze failures and continuously improve the pipeline.

Result
🚀 Deployment time reduced by 60%, accelerating feature releases.
🚀 Deployment success rate increased to 98%, minimizing production issues.
🚀 Developers received real-time feedback, improving code quality and collaboration.
🚀 Standardized processes ensured smooth onboarding for new engineers.

Reflections & What I Would Do Differently
🔹 Implement feature flagging earlier to enable safer rollouts.
🔹 Enhance test coverage metrics to identify potential gaps.
🔹 Introduce AI-driven observability tools for proactive issue detection.

By automating deployments, we streamlined the SDLC, improved efficiency, and fostered a culture of collaboration and continuous improvement at CBA. 🚀
